	  ***	   KLIC version 3     ***
	(prototype version under development)

The KLIC version 3 being developed to enhance functionality and
efficiency of the runtime system of KLIC, to make KLIC a more useful
system for wider range of application.

**********************************************************************
This software is under development and, except for the goal object
feature, features augmented to the original KLIC are not yet ready for
practical use.  Think of it as a pre-alpha version.
**********************************************************************

The current version of the software provides the following features,
in addition to those provided by the original KLIC.

- The Goal Object feature that allows metalevel handling of executable
  goals.

- A tracer, called DDU, written in KL1 itself built upon the goal
  object feature.

- A semiautomatic load distribution mechanism, called SKULD, based on
  lazy task creation concept.

The distribution contains the following files and subdirectories.

  README
    A terse description of what's in the distribution (in Japanese)

  HANDBILL
    Description of the software (in Japanese)

  INFO
    Information on what's where, etc (in Japanese)

  Documents
  Sources
    The directory Documents contains manuals and documents on the
    internal structure of the software.  The directory Sources
    contains source code and sample programs.  Both directories have
    the following subdirectories corresponding  to different parts of
    the software.

      enhanced-klic
	KLIC enhanced with the goal object feature
      ddu
	Tracer written in KL1 itself
      skuld
	Semiautomatic load distribution feature

All the documents except for this very document and those included in
the original KLIC are in Japanese.
